# Verified, but not examples: not compiled into libMutating.a and not tested.
#
# rewrite_array_{nothing,unchanged} are the didactic pair of
# Tutorial/MutatingAndNumeric/Mutating/unchanged.tex.  Both hold the same body,
# a[i] = a[i], and the same postcondition Unchanged{Pre,Post}(a,0,n); they
# differ in one clause, "assigns \nothing" against "assigns a[0..n-1]".
#
# They cannot be ordinary examples: they share the function name, so they would
# collide in a single library.
#
# Expected outcomes differ, and "make check-rewrite-array" asserts both:
#
#   rewrite_array_unchanged  proves completely
#   rewrite_array_nothing    must NOT prove its assigns goal -- unchanged.tex
#                            presents that contract as *incorrect*, because
#                            "assigns \nothing" forbids the write even though
#                            the value written is unchanged
rewrite_array_unchanged
rewrite_array_nothing
